PROP-val-eth-003 — negative control (E)

Adds the consensus-spec upper-bound that grandine is missing in
validate_gossip_rules. With this guard applied, a far-future-slot BeaconBlock
is IGNOREd instead of being buffered into the unbounded delayed_until_slot
BTreeMap, so the flood can no longer grow heap without bound.

Spec: ethereum/consensus-specs p2p-interface.md, beacon_block gossip validation:
  [IGNORE] signed_beacon_block.message.slot
           <= current_slot + MAXIMUM_GOSSIP_CLOCK_DISPARITY_SLOTS

This diff is the A/B control for the harness: build grandine with it applied to
produce the "guarded" variant. If the symptom persists with this applied, the
proposed root cause is wrong (verdict -> FALSE_POSITIVE_RISK).

NOTE: line numbers track the commit pinned in TARGET_INFO.json; rebase the hunk
if the pinned SHA moves.

--- a/fork_choice_store/src/store.rs
+++ b/fork_choice_store/src/store.rs
@@ -1156,6 +1156,14 @@ impl<P: Preset, S: Storage<P>> Store<P, S> {
         // > Blocks cannot be in the future.
         // > If they are, their consideration must be delayed until the are in the past.
         if self.slot() < block.message().slot() {
+            // Negative-control guard for PROP-val-eth-003: the consensus
+            // gossip allowance is 500ms, i.e. less than one 12s devnet slot.
+            // Slot-granular validation therefore must not buffer blocks more
+            // than the next slot into the future.
+            let max_future_slot = self.slot().saturating_add(1);
+            if block.message().slot() > max_future_slot {
+                return Ok(Some(BlockAction::Ignore(false)));
+            }
             return Ok(Some(BlockAction::DelayUntilSlot(block.clone_arc())));
         }
